cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Craton Shield Enterprise"
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Craton Software Company"
    website: "https://github.com/craton-co"
# Cross-checked 2026-05-23: repository-code, license-url, version match
# Cargo.toml workspace metadata (craton-co/craton-shield-enterprise, 0.7.1).
repository-code: "https://github.com/craton-co/craton-shield-enterprise"
license-url: "https://github.com/craton-co/craton-shield-enterprise/blob/main/LICENSE"
version: "0.7.1"
# TODO(maintainers): verify date against signed tag at release time.
# No `v0.7.1` git tag exists in this repository as of 2026-05-23, so the
# date below cannot be cross-checked against a tagger/creator date. The
# value mirrors the CHANGELOG entry for 0.7.1; update both together if
# the signed release tag carries a different commit date.
date-released: "2026-03-28"
abstract: >-
  Production-hardened vehicle cybersecurity runtime with hardware-backed
  cryptography (PKCS#11, TPM 2.0), QNX RTOS support, and fleet telemetry.
  Designed for ISO/SAE 21434, UN R155, and ISO 26262 ASIL-B compliance.
keywords:
  - automotive-cybersecurity
  - embedded-security
  - no-std
  - rust
  - pkcs11
  - tpm
  - iso-21434
  - iso-26262
